ing a Harmonious Campus Emergency Contacts and Useful Telephone Numbers Professional Personal Consultation Service Printable Version Graduate Teaching Assistant in the Department of Management (Appointment for 12 months with possibility of extension) [Ref. T/144/26] The Department of Management at City University of Hong Kong invites applications for the position of Graduate Teaching Assistant (GTA). This is a 12-month appointment with the possibility of extension subject to performance and operational needs. Duties The appointee will provide comprehensive support to the Department in programme administration, teaching-related activities, and student engagement initiatives. Key responsibilities include: Assisting in programme-related activities, including admission interviews, student selection processes, and applicant communications; Supporting programme promotion initiatives such as preparing promotional materials, updating digital content, and coordinating outreach activities; Assisting faculty members with course-related administrative tasks; Coordinating and organising student activities, seminars, talks, workshops, and other academic or co‑curricular events; Liaising with students, faculty members, and external stakeholders as required; Preparing reports, presentation materials, and documentation for departmental use; Providing on-site logistical support during events and activities; and Performing any other duties as assigned by the Department. The appointee is expected to work collaboratively with academic and administrative staff to ensure the smooth operation of departmental programmes and activities. Requirements A Master’s/Bachelor’s degree; Excellent command of written and spoken English; Strong organisational, communication, and interpersonal skills; Proficiency in common office applications (e.g., MS Office and some common AI softwares); and Knowledge of graphic design and image-processing software (e.g., Canva or similar AI tools). Relevant professional and/or teaching experience in tertiary education or a related environment is preferred. Experience in event organisation, programme promotion, and student engagement activities is highly desirable. Candidates with a proactive attitude, strong attention to detail, and the ability to work independently as well as part of a team will be particularly valued. Salary and Conditions of Service Salary offered will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental consultations at the campus clinic. Information and Application Further information on the post and the University is available at http://www.cityu.edu.hk , or from the Human Resources Office, City University of Hong Kong, Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong [Email : hrojob@cityu.edu.hk /Fax : 2788 1154 or 3442 0311]. To apply, please submit an online application . Review of applications will start from 17 August 2026 and will continue until the post is filled and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The University’s privacy policy is available on the homepage. City University of Hong Kong is an  equal opportunity employer. We are committed to the principle of diversity.  Personal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other  employment-related purposes. Best Global Universities Rankings #47 (U.S.News & World Report 2026-2027);  World University Rankings #73 (THE 2026); #1 in the World’s Most International  Universities (THE 2024, 2025 & 2026); Young University Rankings #4 (THE 2024);  Asia University Rankings #14 (THE 2026) and #7 (QS 2026) Services Staff Directory Director of Human Resources Associate Director of Human Resources Team A Team B Team C Team D DT Team Careers Current Openings Senior Management / Deanship / Headship Positions Academic Faculty and Teaching Administrative & Services Research Positions Internal Openings Useful Information How to Apply Online Application Procedures Application 