    "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/hro/en/job/current/academic.asp?ref=uac-r23726": {
      "title": "Human Resources Office",
      "description": "Human Resources Office - City University of Hong Kong Skip to navigation Skip to content Search Search Search - + Human Resources Office Services Staff Directory Director of Human Resources Associate Director of Human Resources Team A Team B Team C Team D DT Team Careers Current Openings Senior Management / Deanship / Headship Positions Academic Faculty and Teaching Administrative & Services Research Positions Internal Openings Useful Information How to Apply Online Application Procedures Application Form for Specified Posts FAQs Prospective Employees' Guide Introduction Living in Hong Kong Banking Children Education Climate Culture, Sports and Leisure Dining Foreign Domestic Helpers Hong Kong Currency Hong Kong Identity Card Housing Octopus Card Shopping Taxation Telecommunication Transportation Work Visa and Dependant Visa Working at City University of Hong Kong Appointees for Faculty Positions Appointees for  Teaching Positions Appointees for  Administrative & Services Positions Staff Only Ex-staff Only Staff Social Club About Staff Social Club Suggestions/Enquiries Upcoming Activities/Events Interest Classes Talks Festive Celebrations Staff Recognition Functions Charity Events/Volunteer Services Visits Gatherings/Outings Sports Events Dance/Tai Chi/Yoga Classes Other Events on Campus Past Activities/Events Photo Gallery Staff Welfare Breastfeeding Room Privileges/Discounts Health Tips and Reminders Current Openings Senior Management / Deanship / Headship Positions Academic Faculty and Teaching Administrative & Services Research Positions Internal Openings Useful Information How to Apply Online Application Procedures Application Form for Specified Posts FAQs Human Resources Office Tel (852) 3442 9250 Fax (852) 3442 0311 (852) 2788 1154 Email hrojob@cityu.edu.hk Office Hours Mon - Fri: 8:45 a.m. - 5:50 p.m. Addr 17/F, Lau Ming Wai Academic Building, City University of HK, 83 Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, HK How to find us? Useful Links Creating a Harmonious Campus Emergency Contacts and Useful Telephone Numbers Professional Personal Consultation Service Printable Version Chair Professor/Professor/Associate  Professor/Assistant Professor (Climate Science/Nature-based Solutions) in the School of Energy and  Environment [Ref. R/237/26] City University of Hong Kong (CityUHK) is one of the world’s leading  universities, known for innovation, creativity and research.  We are now seeking exceptional scholars to  join us as Assistant Professors/Associate Professors/Professors/Chair  Professors (on substantiation-track) in all academic fields with special  focuses on One Health, Digital Society, Smart City, Matter, Brain , and  related interdisciplinary areas.  Research  fields of particular interest include, but not limited to: biomedical  science and engineering veterinary  science computer  science and data science neuroscience  and neural engineering bio-statistics  and AI-healthcare smart/semi-conductor  manufacturing AI/robotics/autonomous  systems aerospace  and microelectronics engineering energy  generation and storage digital  business and innovation management fintech  and business analytics computational  social sciences digital  humanities digital  and new media law  and technology private  law healthy,  smart and sustainable cities Successful candidates should have a demonstrated ability to build a  world-class research programme related to CityUHK’s strategic research areas,  plus a commitment to education and student mentorship.  Candidates must possess a doctorate in their  respective field by the time of appointment. ******************** The School of Energy and Environment was  established at City University of Hong Kong in July 2009 with the mission  to drive interdisciplinary research and education in sustainability, energy,  environment, and climate to cultivate visionary leaders and deliver solutions  for a rapidly decarbonizing, resilient future.   For details of the School of Energy and Environment, please visit the  website at http://www.cityu.edu.hk/see . The School of Energy and Environment is  recruiting leading scholars committed to making impactful contributions to  fundamental and applied research. We are seeking colleagues with a vision for  change who understand the importance of educating the next generation of  environmental leaders and researchers, influencing public policy, and shaping  international agendas. We invite applications for multiple substantiation-track  faculty positions (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor/Chair  Professor) in either Climate Science or Nature-based Solutions (NbS). These are  distinct faculty positions, and candidates may apply to the area that best  aligns with their expertise. Climate Science: priority areas include extreme weather and climate  events, with particular interest in tropical cyclones/typhoons and other  hazards highly relevant to Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area; high-resolution  regional climate modelling and dynamical/statistical downscaling; event  attribution and climate-risk analytics; compound coastal, pluvial and fluvial  flooding; climate impacts, adaptation and resilience; ocean-atmosphere  interactions; monsoon and hydroclimate variability; and data science, AI and  observing systems for climate prediction and early warning. Nature-based Solutions: priority areas include science-led NbS for climate  adaptation and resilience in dense coastal cities; restoration, creation and  management of wetlands, rivers, mangroves, shorelines and other blue-green  infrastructure; urban greening, cooling and stormwater management; biodiversity  enhancement and ecosystem services; ecological engineering and performance  monitoring; and policy, governance, finance and implementation pathways for  mainstreaming NbS in urban development. We are particularly interested in  candidates whose research can support Hong Kong’s emerging NbS agenda to  integrate urban development, ecological conservation, biodiversity enhancement  and climate resilience. These substantiation-track positions  support the strategic development of the School of Energy and Environment.  Across both areas, the School has a particular interest in candidates who  leverage advances in artificial intelligence, machine learning, digital twins,  Earth observation, robotics, autonomous sensing and big-data analytics to  address pressing climate and environmental challenges. In addition, the School  welcomes research that involves field observation, laboratory experimentation  and/or theoretical modeling. The successful candidates are expected to  develop a vigorous, externally funded research program and provide excellence  in teaching at all levels. The successful candidates are encouraged to  collaborate with colleagues from other disciplines within the School of Energy  and Environment to conduct interdisciplinary research and educational  activities to advance the strategic research areas of City University of Hong  Kong. For example, the School collaborates with the State Key Laboratory of  Marine Environmental Health ( https://www.cityu.edu.hk/sklmeh/ ) to  pursue interdisciplinary studies related to ocean science and water research. Duties Conduct international quality research and  develop new research directions. Teach at both undergraduate and postgraduate  levels and supervise research students at master and doctoral levels.  Contribute creatively and professionally in the School, and for the benefit of  the community and industry. The appointees will also be assigned administrative  duties to facilitate the development of the School activities. Requirements A PhD in a closely related discipline  with a strong research record in terms of grants, publications, and/or patents,  along with demonstrated teaching ability. Candidates for Chair Professor and Professor should have outstanding research track records and an international reputation  in the field and demonstrated academic leadership experience. Candidates for Associate Professor should have a sustained record of high-impact  publications and successful grant acquisition and should demonstrate the  ability to lead and develop an independent research program. Candidates for Assistant Professor should have demonstrated potential for  high-impact publication and competitive grant capture. Increasingly, candidates  at this level may already possess several high-quality publications and early  grant success; such achievements are welcome and will be duly considered in the  evaluation process. Candidates are encouraged to describe  their contributions or plans to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion in  academia, and their engagement with societal or policy impact. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be driven by market competitiveness and  individual performance.  Excellent fringe  benefits include gratuity, leave, medical and dental schemes, and relocation  assistance (where applicable).  Initial  appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract. Information and Application Further  information on the posts and the University is available at http://www.cityu.edu.hk , or from the School of Energy and Environment, City  University of Hong Kong, Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong (email : seedean@cityu.edu.hk ). To  apply, please submit an online application and include a cover letter, with the  curriculum vitae, a detailed research plan (3 pages maximum), a teaching  philosophy statement and plan (2 pages maximum), as well as a list of three  referees. Nominations can be sent directly to the School of Energy and  Environment (email: seedean@cityu.edu.hk ). Review of applications will start from 7 August 2026,  and will continue until the posts are filled .  Only  shortlisted applicants will be contacted; and those shortlisted for the post of  Assistant Professor will be requested to arrange for at least 2 reference  reports sent directly by the referees to the Department, specifying the  position applied for.  The University's privacy policy is available on the homepage. City University of Hong Kong is an  equal opportunity employer. We are committed to the principle of diversity.  Personal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other  employment-related purposes. Best Global Universities Rankings #47 (U.S.News & World Report 2026-2027);  World University Rankings #73 (THE 2026); #1 in the World’s Most International  Universities (THE 2024, 2025 & 2026); Young University Rankings #4 (THE 2024);  Asia University Rankings #14 (THE 2026) and #7 (QS 2026) Services Staff Directory Director of Human Resources Associate Director of Human Resources Team A Team B Team C Team D DT Team Careers Current Openings Senior Management / Deanship / Headship Positions Academic Faculty and Teaching Administrative & Services Research Positions Internal Openings Useful Information How to Apply Online Application Procedures Application Form for Specified Posts FAQs Prospective Employees' Guide Introduction Living in Hong Kong Banking Children Education Climate Culture, Sports and Leisure Dining Foreign Domestic Helpers Hong Kong Currency Hong Kong Identity Card Housing Octopus Card Shopping Taxation Telecommunication Transportation Work Visa and Dependant Visa Working at City University of Hong Kong Appointees for Faculty Positions Appointees for  Teaching Positions Appointees for  Administrative & Services Positions Staff Only Ex-staff Only Staff Social Club About Staff Social Club Suggestions/Enquiries Upcoming Activities/Events Interest Classes Talks Festive Celebrations Staff Recognition Functions Charity Events/Volunteer Services Visits Gatherings/Outings Sports Events Dance/Tai Chi/Yoga Classes Other Events on Campus Past Activities/Events Photo Gallery Staff Welfare Breastfeeding Room Privileges/Discounts Health Tips and Reminders Privacy Policy · Copyright · Disclaimer · Accessibility · Contact Us · 