ing a Harmonious Campus Emergency Contacts and Useful Telephone Numbers Professional Personal Consultation Service Printable Version Professor/Associate Professor of Practice in the Department of Management [Ref. T/073/26] Duties We are seeking an exceptional program leader with profound expertise across interdisciplinary fields—AI, business transformation, disruptive technologies, entrepreneurship, geopolitics, and global business strategy. We are looking for a visionary to drive the establishment and strategic direction of a new cross disciplinary framework, integrating cutting edge theory with real world practice to foster innovative academic collaboration. The successful candidate will lead programme development, teaching, and strategic leadership within an interdisciplinary postgraduate environment. The appointee will be based in the Department of Management pending the formal launch of the new unit. Key Responsibilities: Contribute to the strategic development of new University-wide initiatives in executive and interdisciplinary postgraduate education; Oversee postgraduate programmes, ensuring quality for both executive-level and early career professionals; Lead curriculum innovation, bridging theory, practice, and cross-disciplinary perspectives; Identify and engage adjunct faculty and distinguished guest speakers from industry; Deliver lectures, providing students with practical insights; Spearhead programme marketing and student recruitment; Manage daily administration and class operations; and Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements Candidates must have a doctoral degree. The successful candidate should have a minimum of 10 years of experience in relevant fields. Teaching experience at postgraduate and executive levels is advantageous. Demonstrated leadership and contribution to the profession, industry, or academic community. Based in Hong Kong with occasional travel to the Chinese Mainland. Able to commence duty as soon as possible. Salary and Conditions of Service Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract; fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental schemes. Information and Application Further information on the posts and the University is available at http://www.cityu.edu.hk , or from the Human Resources Office, City University of Hong Kong, Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong [Email : hrojob@cityu.edu.hk /Fax : 2788 1154 or 3442 0311]. To apply, please submit an online application. Applications will receive full consideration until the positions are filled and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The University’s privacy policy is available on the homepage. City University of Hong Kong is an  equal opportunity employer. We are committed to the principle of diversity.  Personal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other  employment-related purposes. Best Global Universities Rankings #47 (U.S.News & World Report 2026-2027);  World University Rankings #73 (THE 2026); #1 in the World’s Most International  Universities (THE 2024, 2025 & 2026); Young University Rankings #4 (THE 2024);  Asia University Rankings #14 (THE 2026) and #7 (QS 2026) Services Staff Directory Director of Human Resources Associate Director of Human Resources Team A Team B Team C Team D DT Team Careers Current Openings Senior Management / Deanship / Headship Positions Academic Faculty and Teaching Administrative & Services Research Positions Internal Openings Useful Information How to Apply Online Application Procedures Application Form for Specified Posts FAQs Prospective Employees' Guide Introduction Living in Hong Kong Banking Children Education Climate Culture, Sports and Leisure Dining Foreign Domestic Helpers Hong Kong Currency Hong Kong Identity Card Housing Octopus Card Shopping Taxation Telecommunication Transportation Work Visa and Dependant Visa Working at City University of Hong 