ing a Harmonious Campus Emergency Contacts and Useful Telephone Numbers Professional Personal Consultation Service Printable Version Part-time Lecturers in the Department of Data Science [Ref. T/099/25] Duties To teach any of the postgraduate course(s) in Semester A (commencing early September) and/or Semester B (commencing mid-January). Postgraduate courses include but not limited to the following: SDSC6012 – Time Series and Recurrent Neural Networks SDSC6016 – Predictive Analytics and Financial Applications SDSC8013 – Statistical Methods for Categorical Data Analysis (For detailed course information, please visit the website: https://www.ds.cityu.edu.hk/programmes/postgraduate-programmes/msds ) Duties may also include conducting tutorials, supervision of students in laboratory work, marking of assignments, setting and marking of examination papers and any other work as assigned by the Head of Department. Teaching duties will be carried out during daytime, in the evening and weekend throughout the academic year. Requirements A PhD degree in related disciplines with proven teaching experience at the university level is required. Salary and Conditions of Service Salary offered will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information and Application Further information on the posts and the University is available at http://www.cityu.edu.hk , or from the Human Resources Office, City University of Hong Kong, Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong [Email : hrojob@cityu.edu.hk /Fax : 2788 1154 or 3442 0311]. To apply, please submit an online application. Applications will receive full consideration until the positions are filled and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The University’s privacy policy is available on the homepage. City University of Hong Kong is an  equal opportunity employer. We are committed to the principle of diversity.  Personal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other  employment-r