ing a Harmonious Campus Emergency Contacts and Useful Telephone Numbers Professional Personal Consultation Service Printable Version Teaching Consultant in the Department of Media and Communication (Appointment for 24 months) [Ref. B/R/1340/09] Duties Teach undergraduate and/or postgraduate courses in the fields of communication, and public relations, including evening classes for postgraduate courses; Organise programmes, events and activities to enrich students’ learning experience; Initiate and implement department-wide publicity and promotion programmes to enhance the branding and image of the Department; Initiate professional engagement, networking and outreach activities to enhance the academic and professional reputation of the Department; Coordinate and coach students to join various competitions/contests; and Perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or the delegates. Requirements A relevant Master’s degree or above, with rich experience in media or public relations-related industry is required. Preference will be given to those with teaching experience at university level in the related areas. Salary and Conditions of Service Salary offered will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information and Application Further information on the post and the University is available at http://www.cityu.edu.hk , or from the Department of Media and Communication, City University of Hong Kong, Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong [Email: com@cityu.edu.hk ]. To apply, please submit an online application  and include a current curriculum vitae and supporting documents. Applications will receive full consideration until the position is filled and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The University’s privacy policy is available on the homepage. City University of Hong Kong is an  equal opportunity employer. We are committed to the principle of diversity.  Personal data provided by applicants will be used 